WEBVTT

00:00:09.083 --> 00:00:11.583
Ah. Thank you.

00:00:11.708 --> 00:00:12.833
Officer.

00:00:14.958 --> 00:00:15.958
Hmm.

00:00:17.542 --> 00:00:21.000
So, about the authorities.
I've printed off directions.

00:00:21.083 --> 00:00:22.292
Oh. Laminated.

00:00:22.375 --> 00:00:24.542
- The green arrows are to make...
- Thank you, darling.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.292
I know exactly where I'm going.

00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:28.667
- Where's Paddington?
- What?

00:00:29.375 --> 00:00:30.625
Oh! Paddington.

00:00:30.708 --> 00:00:32.125
Paddington!

00:00:33.958 --> 00:00:35.417
Hmm...

00:00:38.708 --> 00:00:39.792
Oh!

00:00:44.542 --> 00:00:45.583
I-Hmm!

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:48.042
♪ Wow, I feel good

00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:51.500
♪ I knew that I would now

00:00:53.375 --> 00:00:55.375
♪ I feel good

00:00:56.333 --> 00:00:58.417
♪ I knew that I would now

00:01:00.042 --> 00:01:01.250
♪ So good

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.292
♪ So good

00:01:03.375 --> 00:01:05.333
♪ I got you

00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:07.917
Paddington?

00:01:08.042 --> 00:01:09.542
Paddington!

00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:12.042
- Over here!
- Coming.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:29.208
That one's mine, thank you.

00:01:30.125 --> 00:01:32.917
I assume he's yours.

00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:35.333
Tell you what, Paddington.

00:01:35.375 --> 00:01:39.375
It's not far to my friend's
antiques shop. Why don't we walk?

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:44.833
- Ah, Mrs Brown. Come in.
- You must be Mr Gruber.

00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:48.792
And you must be the young gentleman
whose hat sounds so fascinating.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.292
Welcome. You're just in time
for elevenses.

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:16.625
Every morning it arrives at 11 o'clock,

00:02:16.708 --> 00:02:18.875
bringing salvation.

00:02:18.958 --> 00:02:22.250
Just like a train that I took
many years ago.

00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:24.792
- Really?
- Oh, yes. You see,

00:02:24.875 --> 00:02:27.542
there was a lot of trouble
in my country.

00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:32.208
So my parents sent me
all the way across Europe,

00:02:32.292 --> 00:02:35.375
when I was not much older
than you are now.

00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:39.542
Was it hard to find a home?

00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:41.875
I had a great-aunt who took me in.

00:02:42.458 --> 00:02:44.125
Master Gruber?

00:02:44.708 --> 00:02:49.417
But I soon learnt a home
is more than a roof over your head.

00:02:55.083 --> 00:02:59.292
My body had travelled very fast
but my heart...

00:03:00.292 --> 00:03:03.292
she took a little longer to arrive.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.417
Hmm.

00:03:05.542 --> 00:03:08.000
But now I should like
to take a look at your hat.

00:03:08.083 --> 00:03:10.750
- Oh, thank you.
- Unusual colour.

00:03:10.833 --> 00:03:15.042
But it is hard to say how much of that
is original and how much...

00:03:16.042 --> 00:03:17.542
Marmalade?

00:03:17.625 --> 00:03:20.167
My uncle always kept
a marmalade sandwich in his hat

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.792
in case of emergency.

00:03:21.875 --> 00:03:26.000
You're pulling my legs off.
What a splendid idea.

00:03:26.083 --> 00:03:29.083
Ooh. Now, if you look carefully,

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:31.417
you can see your hat
has been hand stitched,

00:03:31.542 --> 00:03:33.708
which suggests it is one of a kind.

00:03:33.792 --> 00:03:35.167
- Really?
- Yes.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:36.292
Hello there.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:42.417
- Oh, wait a minute.
- It's very subtle.

00:03:42.542 --> 00:03:45.375
- Oh, Paddington!
- The gentleman dropped his wallet!

00:03:46.375 --> 00:03:47.917
Where is he?

00:03:48.042 --> 00:03:49.958
- Mind out!
- Stop!

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.917
Come back!

00:03:53.708 --> 00:03:55.250
What's he doing?

00:03:55.917 --> 00:03:58.250
- Excuse me. Coming through.
- Careful!

00:03:58.292 --> 00:04:00.458
Just trying to return
some lost property.

00:04:00.583 --> 00:04:02.208
Hey, what are you doing?

00:04:04.417 --> 00:04:05.667
Whoa!

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.875
Sorry!

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.250
Oi, come back!

00:04:14.083 --> 00:04:16.625
Some kind of tiny police bear.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.875
You!

00:04:25.958 --> 00:04:27.208
What are you doing?

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:30.000
Trying to return some lost property.

00:04:30.083 --> 00:04:33.292
Get away from here! Leave my dog alone!

00:04:36.917 --> 00:04:38.125
Do you want a biscuit?

00:04:38.208 --> 00:04:42.375
Charlie Delta. Officer in distress.
Urgent assistance required. Go, go, go.

00:04:49.958 --> 00:04:52.375
In 100 yards, bear left.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.875
I've got your wallet!

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:03.500
Whoa-hum

00:05:03.583 --> 00:05:06.125
It's actually quite good fun. Ah.

00:05:11.125 --> 00:05:12.750
The Winter's Tale

00:05:12.875 --> 00:05:15.875
contains Shakespeare's
most famous stage direction:

00:05:15.958 --> 00:05:19.083
- "Exit, pursued by a..."
- Paddington?

00:05:19.125 --> 00:05:21.542
- Paddington?
- Look, a bear!

00:05:31.292 --> 00:05:33.292
You... dropped your wallet.

00:05:34.583 --> 00:05:36.750
Gosh, you've got quite a few.

00:05:37.458 --> 00:05:39.083
He certainly has.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:47.542
No, you don't understand. I was just
trying to return some lost property.

00:05:48.042 --> 00:05:49.833
Oh, hello, Judy.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.458
- Do you know that bear?
- Erm...

00:05:53.542 --> 00:05:54.875
He's awesome.

00:05:55.708 --> 00:05:58.375
- Yeah, he's called Paddington.
- Thank you.

00:05:59.583 --> 00:06:00.917
Thank you.

00:06:01.083 --> 00:06:03.083
- Well done.
- Bear of the moment!

00:06:03.125 --> 00:06:06.208
Oh, really? I just did
what any bear would do.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:07.708
I can't thank you enough.

00:06:07.792 --> 00:06:11.625
That scoundrel has been pocket-picketing
people around here for weeks.

00:06:11.708 --> 00:06:13.125
He was extraordinary.

00:06:13.167 --> 00:06:15.625
And it gave me
a chance to look at his hat.

00:06:16.125 --> 00:06:18.792
- You see, this is no ordinary hat.
- No?

00:06:18.875 --> 00:06:24.750
No. These markings mean that it was made
for a member of the Geographers' Guild.

00:06:24.833 --> 00:06:26.042
What's that?

00:06:26.125 --> 00:06:28.375
A very old explorers' club.

00:06:28.458 --> 00:06:30.375
- Oh!
- Go and see them in the morning,

00:06:30.458 --> 00:06:33.000
and if luck has been smiling
on your face,

00:06:33.083 --> 00:06:35.583
they should be able to tell you
who they made it for.

00:06:37.333 --> 00:06:39.833
OK. Protein.

00:06:39.917 --> 00:06:41.875
- Per biscuit?
- Per biscuit.

00:06:41.958 --> 00:06:45.167
- 0.5 grams.
- Yes.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.125
Carbohydrates.

00:06:48.208 --> 00:06:49.792
- Per biscuit?
- Per biscuit.

00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:53.625
- Is 7.7 grams.
- Yes.

00:06:55.125 --> 00:06:58.208
- Sodium.
- Ooh...

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:00.667
- I know this one.
- Yeah. Do you?

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:02.958
- Is it trace?
- Not trace.

